WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.000
Here's the healthcare paradox Washington still cannot explain.

2
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:14.900
Puerto Rico receives 41% less Medicare funding than the states, yet it continues to deliver

3
00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:19.520
some of the strongest Medicare Advantage quality results in the nation.

4
00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:21.520
How is that possible?

5
00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:25.880
And if Puerto Rico can achieve these results while being funded at such a disadvantage,

6
00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:29.840
imagine what it could accomplish if Washington funded it fairly.

7
00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:33.440
That is exactly what The Healthcare Paradox explores.

8
00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:41.200
Real data, real outcomes, real federal policy explained in plain English, no Washington jargon,

9
00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:45.840
no political spin, just the numbers, the results and the facts behind Puerto Rico's health

10
00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:48.120
care funding disparity.

11
00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:50.360
Because this is bigger than Puerto Rico.

12
00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:54.440
It is about what happens when actual healthcare performance exposes the flaws in a

13
00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:58.920
federal funding formula that simply does not match the results.

14
00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:04.960
Less funding, exceptional performance, an unequal formula, follow the numbers, look

15
00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:06.880
at the results.

16
00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:10.640
Then ask the question Washington still has not answered.

17
00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:13.720
Why is Puerto Rico still being funded differently?

18
00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:15.560
The Healthcare Paradox.

19
00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:17.720
New episodes are out now.

20
00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:24.200
Listen on Amazon Music, Apple Podcasts, Spotify, iHeartRadio and YouTube or wherever you

21
00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:25.520
listen to your podcasts.
